'''Matngele''' or '''Madngele''' is an extinct [[Australian Aboriginal languages|Australian Aboriginal language]] of the [[Northern Territory]] spoken by the [[Madngella]] and [[Yunggor]] peoples.

==Classification==
Tryon (1974) classified Matngele with [[Kamu language|Kamu]], and this is accepted by Dixon (2002) and Bowern (2011), though denied by Harvey (1990).<ref name="AIATSIS"/>

